  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given line <math><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math><br />Circle <math><mi>S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p>Centre <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> Radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math><br />Now, the line will be tangent to the circle<br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> <math><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></math><br /><math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>19</mn></math><br />So, for only one point of intersection inequality,&nbsp;<math><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math> must not satisfy the centre of the circle<br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></math></p>"
  }
